{"type":"message","id":"15897eb2","parentId":"398b5045","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:08:42.041Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think about the optimal solution for handling compressed memory files. The current approach compresses files older than 30 days into .gz format. But this makes them hard to search.\n\nThe optimal solution would be:\n1. Keep a searchable index of all memory files (compressed or not)\n2. Use a vector database or full-text search for semantic search\n3. When searching, decompress on-the-fly if needed\n\nLet me check if there's a memory search function in OpenClaw.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ada65344531445de83d78dc2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"memory_search\\|memory.*search\" /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/ 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":120,"output":255,"cacheRead":86720,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87095,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779818915078}}
{"type":"message","id":"4bb96ab3","parentId":"15897eb2","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:08:42.406Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ada65344531445de83d78dc2","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/Gemini: add `gemini-embedding-2-preview` memory-search support with configurable output dimensions and automatic reindexing when the configured dimensions change. (#42501) Thanks @BillChirico and @gumadeiras.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/memory teardown: close cached memory search/index managers in the one-shot CLI shutdown path so watcher-backed memory caches no longer keep completed CLI runs alive after output finishes. (#40389) thanks @Julbarth.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD Windows: fail closed when `qmd.cmd` or `mcporter.cmd` wrappers cannot be resolved to a direct entrypoint, so memory search no longer falls back to shell execution on Windows.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/Gemini: normalize returned Gemini embeddings across direct query, direct batch, and async batch paths so memory search uses consistent vector handling for Gemini too. (#43409) Thanks @gumadeiras.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD mcporter Windows spawn hardening: when `mcporter.cmd` launch fails with `spawn EINVAL`, retry via bare `mcporter` shell resolution so QMD recall can continue instead of falling back to builtin memory search. (#27402) Thanks @i0ivi0i.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD search result decoding: accept `qmd search` hits that only include `file` URIs (for example `qmd://collection/path.md`) without `docid`, resolve them through managed collection roots, and keep multi-collection results keyed by file fallback so valid QMD hits no longer collapse to empty `memory_search` output. (#28181) Thanks @0x76696265.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD collection safety: stop destructive collection rebinds when QMD `collection list` only reports names without path metadata, preventing `memory search` from dropping existing collections if re-add fails. (#36870) Thanks @Adnannnnnnna.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/doctor SecretRef handling: treat SecretRef-backed memory-search API keys as configured, and fail embedding setup with explicit unresolved-secret errors instead of crashing. (#36835) Thanks @joshavant.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/Docs memory help accuracy: clarify `openclaw memory status --deep` behavior and align memory command examples/docs with the current search options. (#31803) Thanks @JasonOA888 and @Avi974.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/Memory search: accept `--query <text>` for `openclaw memory search` (while keeping positional query support), and emit a clear error when neither form is provided. (#25904, #25857) Thanks @niceysam and @stakeswky."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":360,"aggregated":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/Gemini: add `gemini-embedding-2-preview` memory-search support with configurable output dimensions and automatic reindexing when the configured dimensions change. (#42501) Thanks @BillChirico and @gumadeiras.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/memory teardown: close cached memory search/index managers in the one-shot CLI shutdown path so watcher-backed memory caches no longer keep completed CLI runs alive after output finishes. (#40389) thanks @Julbarth.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD Windows: fail closed when `qmd.cmd` or `mcporter.cmd` wrappers cannot be resolved to a direct entrypoint, so memory search no longer falls back to shell execution on Windows.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/Gemini: normalize returned Gemini embeddings across direct query, direct batch, and async batch paths so memory search uses consistent vector handling for Gemini too. (#43409) Thanks @gumadeiras.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD mcporter Windows spawn hardening: when `mcporter.cmd` launch fails with `spawn EINVAL`, retry via bare `mcporter` shell resolution so QMD recall can continue instead of falling back to builtin memory search. (#27402) Thanks @i0ivi0i.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD search result decoding: accept `qmd search` hits that only include `file` URIs (for example `qmd://collection/path.md`) without `docid`, resolve them through managed collection roots, and keep multi-collection results keyed by file fallback so valid QMD hits no longer collapse to empty `memory_search` output. (#28181) Thanks @0x76696265.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/QMD collection safety: stop destructive collection rebinds when QMD `collection list` only reports names without path metadata, preventing `memory search` from dropping existing collections if re-add fails. (#36870) Thanks @Adnannnnnnna.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- Memory/doctor SecretRef handling: treat SecretRef-backed memory-search API keys as configured, and fail embedding setup with explicit unresolved-secret errors instead of crashing. (#36835) Thanks @joshavant.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/Docs memory help accuracy: clarify `openclaw memory status --deep` behavior and align memory command examples/docs with the current search options. (#31803) Thanks @JasonOA888 and @Avi974.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/CHANGELOG.md:- CLI/Memory search: accept `--query <text>` for `openclaw memory search` (while keeping positional query support), and emit a clear error when neither form is provided. (#25904, #25857) Thanks @niceysam and @stakeswky.","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779818922404}}
