{"type":"message","id":"208dc8b8","parentId":"83b7820b","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:42:48.619Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check if OpenClaw's memory search can index session transcripts.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8f97f0c2e60942ba8e3fe715","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md | grep -A 10 -i \"session\\|transcript\" | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":490,"output":87,"cacheRead":73600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74177,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779820958999}}
{"type":"message","id":"66ee898e","parentId":"208dc8b8","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:42:48.631Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8f97f0c2e60942ba8e3fe715","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"- Read today + yesterday at session start.\n- `MEMORY.md` (optional)\n  - Curated long-term memory.\n  - **Only load in the main, private session** (never in group contexts).\n\nThese files live under the workspace (`agents.defaults.workspace`, default\n`~/.openclaw/workspace`). See [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace) for the full layout.\n\n## Memory tools\n\nOpenClaw exposes two agent-facing tools for these Markdown files:\n\n- `memory_search` — semantic recall over indexed snippets.\n- `memory_get` — targeted read of a specific Markdown file/line range.\n--\nWhen a session is **close to auto-compaction**, OpenClaw triggers a **silent,\nagentic turn** that reminds the model to write durable memory **before** the\ncontext is compacted. The default prompts explicitly say the model _may reply_,\nbut usually `NO_REPLY` is the correct response so the user never sees this turn.\n\nThis is controlled by `agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`:\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n--\n          systemPrompt: \"Session nearing compaction. Store durable memories now.\",\n          prompt: \"Write any lasting notes to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; reply with NO_REPLY if nothing to store.\",\n        },"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":8,"aggregated":"- Read today + yesterday at session start.\n- `MEMORY.md` (optional)\n  - Curated long-term memory.\n  - **Only load in the main, private session** (never in group contexts).\n\nThese files live under the workspace (`agents.defaults.workspace`, default\n`~/.openclaw/workspace`). See [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace) for the full layout.\n\n## Memory tools\n\nOpenClaw exposes two agent-facing tools for these Markdown files:\n\n- `memory_search` — semantic recall over indexed snippets.\n- `memory_get` — targeted read of a specific Markdown file/line range.\n--\nWhen a session is **close to auto-compaction**, OpenClaw triggers a **silent,\nagentic turn** that reminds the model to write durable memory **before** the\ncontext is compacted. The default prompts explicitly say the model _may reply_,\nbut usually `NO_REPLY` is the correct response so the user never sees this turn.\n\nThis is controlled by `agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`:\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n--\n          systemPrompt: \"Session nearing compaction. Store durable memories now.\",\n          prompt: \"Write any lasting notes to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; reply with NO_REPLY if nothing to store.\",\n        },","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779820968629}}
{"type":"message","id":"fba00c34","parentId":"66ee898e","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:42:58.494Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check if session transcripts are indexed by memory search.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e9b8024cfeb94a9a9743f5e0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md | grep -B 5 -A 15 \"extraPaths\\|transcript\" | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":392,"output":84,"cacheRead":74048,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":74524,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779820968632}}
{"type":"message","id":"06029ebe","parentId":"fba00c34","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:42:58.507Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e9b8024cfeb94a9a9743f5e0","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`channel`/`chatType` so empty results are easier to debug.\n- Snippets sourced outside the workspace show up as\n  `qmd/<collection>/<relative-path>` in `memory_search` results; `memory_get`\n  understands that prefix and reads from the configured QMD collection root.\n- When `memory.qmd.sessions.enabled = true`, OpenClaw exports sanitized session\n  transcripts (User/Assistant turns) into a dedicated QMD collection under\n  `~/.openclaw/agents/<id>/qmd/sessions/`, so `memory_search` can recall recent\n  conversations without touching the builtin SQLite index.\n- `memory_search` snippets now include a `Source: <path#line>` footer when\n  `memory.citations` is `auto`/`on`; set `memory.citations = \"off\"` to keep\n  the path metadata internal (the agent still receives the path for\n  `memory_get`, but the snippet text omits the footer and the system prompt\n  warns the agent not to cite it).\n\n**Example**\n\n```json5\nmemory: {\n  backend: \"qmd\",\n  citations: \"auto\",\n  qmd: {\n--\n\n```json5\nagents: {\n  defaults: {\n    memorySearch: {\n      extraPaths: [\"../team-docs\", \"/srv/shared-notes/overview.md\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- Paths can be absolute or workspace-relative.\n- Directories are scanned recursively for `.md` files.\n- By default, only Markdown files are indexed.\n- If `memorySearch.multimodal.enabled = true`, OpenClaw also indexes supported image/audio files under `extraPaths` only. Default memory roots (`MEMORY.md`, `memory.md`, `memory/**/*.md`) stay Markdown-only.\n- Symlinks are ignored (files or directories)."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":8,"aggregated":"`channel`/`chatType` so empty results are easier to debug.\n- Snippets sourced outside the workspace show up as\n  `qmd/<collection>/<relative-path>` in `memory_search` results; `memory_get`\n  understands that prefix and reads from the configured QMD collection root.\n- When `memory.qmd.sessions.enabled = true`, OpenClaw exports sanitized session\n  transcripts (User/Assistant turns) into a dedicated QMD collection under\n  `~/.openclaw/agents/<id>/qmd/sessions/`, so `memory_search` can recall recent\n  conversations without touching the builtin SQLite index.\n- `memory_search` snippets now include a `Source: <path#line>` footer when\n  `memory.citations` is `auto`/`on`; set `memory.citations = \"off\"` to keep\n  the path metadata internal (the agent still receives the path for\n  `memory_get`, but the snippet text omits the footer and the system prompt\n  warns the agent not to cite it).\n\n**Example**\n\n```json5\nmemory: {\n  backend: \"qmd\",\n  citations: \"auto\",\n  qmd: {\n--\n\n```json5\nagents: {\n  defaults: {\n    memorySearch: {\n      extraPaths: [\"../team-docs\", \"/srv/shared-notes/overview.md\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNotes:\n\n- Paths can be absolute or workspace-relative.\n- Directories are scanned recursively for `.md` files.\n- By default, only Markdown files are indexed.\n- If `memorySearch.multimodal.enabled = true`, OpenClaw also indexes supported image/audio files under `extraPaths` only. Default memory roots (`MEMORY.md`, `memory.md`, `memory/**/*.md`) stay Markdown-only.\n- Symlinks are ignored (files or directories).","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779820978505}}
{"type":"message","id":"e78f7973","parentId":"06029ebe","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:43:04.559Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand. The key insight is:\n\n1. **Session transcripts** (`.jsonl` files in `/workspace/projects/agents/main/sessions/`) are the raw conversation logs\n2. **Session archives** (`.md` files in `memory/sessions/`) are summaries\n3. OpenClaw's memory search can index `memory/*.md` files, and with QMD backend, it can also index session transcripts\n\nThe question is: are session transcripts being indexed? Let me check if they're in the extraPaths config.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1895c6b9f9c245bda3cc1f2f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -A 5 \"extraPaths\" /workspace/projects/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":471,"output":265,"cacheRead":74432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":75168,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779820978507}}
{"type":"message","id":"06f3a851","parentId":"e78f7973","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:43:04.575Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1895c6b9f9c245bda3cc1f2f","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"extraPaths\": [\n          \"/workspace/projects/workspace/chanlun-agent/knowledge\",\n          \"/workspace/projects/workspace/knowledge\"\n        ],\n        \"cache\": {\n          \"enabled\": true"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":9,"aggregated":"\"extraPaths\": [\n          \"/workspace/projects/workspace/chanlun-agent/knowledge\",\n          \"/workspace/projects/workspace/knowledge\"\n        ],\n        \"cache\": {\n          \"enabled\": true","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779820984572}}
{"type":"message","id":"9b119e64","parentId":"06f3a851","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:43:27.052Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the current extraPaths only includes knowledge directories, not session transcripts. Let me check if there's a way to index session transcripts.\n\nThe key question from VAN is:\n1. Can we search session transcripts? (Currently no - they're JSONL, not indexed)\n2. Should sessions be merged into the knowledge base?\n\nLet me provide a clear answer.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Captain，你说得对。当前问题：\n\n## 📊 Session 现状\n\n| 类型 | 位置 | 可搜索 | 大小 |\n|------|------|--------|------|\n| Session归档 | `memory/sessions/*.md` | ✅ grep | ~40KB |\n| Session原始记录 | `agents/main/sessions/*.jsonl` | ❌ | 27MB |\n| 知识库 | `chanlun-agent/knowledge/*.md` | ✅ | ~100KB |\n\n**问题**：27MB 的对话原始记录（JSONL）完全没被索引，搜不到。\n\n## 🔧 解决方案\n\n**方案1：把 session transcripts 加入 extraPaths**\n```json5\nextraPaths: [\n  \"/workspace/projects/workspace/chanlun-agent/knowledge\",\n  \"/workspace/projects/workspace/knowledge\",\n  \"/workspace/projects/agents/main/sessions\"  // 新增\n]\n```\n但 JSONL 不是 Markdown，不会被自动索引。\n\n**方案2：Session 归档时提取精华到知识库**\n```\nsession对话 → 归档(memory/sessions/) → 提取关键知识 → knowledge/\n```\n每段重要对话的结论/决策/教训 → 写入知识库 .md 文件\n\n**方案3：QMD backend + session indexing**\n```json5\nmemory: {\n  backend: \"qmd\",\n  qmd: {\n    sessions: { enabled: true }  // 自动索引session transcripts\n  }\n}\n```\n需要装 QMD (Bun + node-llama-cpp)\n\n## 💡 我的建议\n\n**方案2 最实际** — 现在就能做：\n1. 每次 session 归档时，把关键知识提取到 `knowledge/` 目录\n2. 知识库已有 `extraPaths` 配置，会被自动索引\n3. 不需要装额外软件\n\n要我现在把今天的关键知识（Tiger SDK fixes、交易SOP、订单格式）整理到 knowledge 目录吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":227,"output":590,"cacheRead":74880,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":75697,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779820984576}}
{"type":"message","id":"92ab01ec","parentId":"9b119e64","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:45:06.875Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e6aedd0f960c4eb90762a46fbf\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"sender\": \"VAN\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 02:45 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"VAN (ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"name\": \"VAN\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e6aedd0f960c4eb90762a46fbf]\nVAN: 提取到知识库是生硬的没有上下文啊"}],"timestamp":1779821106872}}
{"type":"message","id":"3b580d65","parentId":"92ab01ec","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:45:28.620Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN is right. Extracting snippets to a knowledge directory loses the conversational context - the back-and-forth, the reasoning chain, the \"why\" behind decisions. A standalone .md file saying \"Tiger SDK fix: use get_contract()\" doesn't capture the debugging process, the error messages, the alternative approaches considered.\n\nVAN wants to be able to search through the actual session transcripts with full context. The real solution is to index the session transcripts directly.\n\nLet me think about what options we actually have:\n\n1. **QMD backend** - Can index session transcripts natively with `qmd.sessions.enabled = true`. But requires Bun + node-llama-cpp installation.\n\n\n2. **Convert JSONL to MD and add to extraPaths** - Write a script that converts .jsonl session files to readable .md format, then add that path to extraPaths. This would work with the current setup.\n3. **Embedding provider + session indexing** - Once we have an embedding provider, we can configure it to index sessions too.\n\nThe core issue is that we need an embedding provider for semantic search to work at all. Without it, we're stuck. The JSONL-to-MD conversion is a practical workaround that lets us grep through sessions now, but it doesn't solve the semantic search problem.\n\nI'm realizing the real constraint: OpenClaw's memory search only indexes files in the configured paths, and the session transcripts live outside that scope. The proper solution is either setting up QMD with session indexing enabled, or getting an embedding provider configured to index sessions directly. Both require infrastructure we don't have yet.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Captain，你说得对。提取出来的知识没有对话上下文，丢失了\"为什么这么做\"的推理过程。\n\n## 真正的解决方案\n\n**直接索引 session transcripts**，保留完整上下文。\n\n有两条路：\n\n### 路线1：QMD backend（推荐）\n```json5\nmemory: { backend: \"qmd\", qmd: { sessions: { enabled: true } } }\n```\n- 自动索引 session JSONL\n- 保留完整对话上下文\n- BM25 + 向量 + reranking\n- **需要**: 装 QMD (Bun + node-llama-cpp)\n\n### 路线2：embedding provider + session路径\n```json5\nmemorySearch: {\n  provider: \"ollama\",\n  extraPaths: [\"/workspace/projects/agents/main/sessions\"]\n}\n```\n- 把 session 路径加到 extraPaths\n- 但 JSONL 不是 MD，不会被索引\n- 需要先转格式\n\n## 本质问题\n\n不管哪条路，**都需要装东西**：\n- QMD → Bun + node-llama-cpp\n- Ollama embedding → Ollama + nomic-embed-text\n\nCaptain，要我现在装哪个？QMD 是 OpenClaw 官方方案，一步到位解决 session 索引问题。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":828,"output":960,"cacheRead":75072,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":76860,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779821106874}}
{"type":"message","id":"7cd39b35","parentId":"3b580d65","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:51:53.031Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e6af24d6ca0c4f3741105bd621\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"sender\": \"VAN\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 02:51 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"VAN (ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"name\": \"VAN\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e6af24d6ca0c4f3741105bd621]\nVAN: 三级全量，session需写入记忆，提取到知识库的并纳入知识库合理结构同时支持直接索引 session transcripts，保留完整上下文。\n\n有两条路："}],"timestamp":1779821513029}}
{"type":"message","id":"df17d9e7","parentId":"7cd39b35","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:52:16.645Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN wants a three-tier memory system:\n\n1. **Session transcripts** - full raw conversation logs (direct indexing)\n2. **Memory files** - daily summaries extracted from sessions\n3. **Knowledge base** - structured knowledge extracted from sessions\n\nAnd he wants all three to work together. Let me think about what he's saying:\n\n- \"三级全量\" = three levels, all-inclusive\n- \"session需写入记忆\" = sessions need to be written to memory\n- \"提取到知识库的并纳入知识库合理结构\" = extracted knowledge should be integrated into knowledge base proper structure\n\n\n- \"同时支持直接索引 session transcripts，保留完整上下文\" = simultaneously support direct indexing of session transcripts, preserving full context\n\nSo the architecture is: raw session logs as the foundation, daily memory summaries as the middle layer, and structured knowledge at the top—all three searchable and indexed. He's asking which path to take for implementation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"明白了 Captain。三级记忆架构：\n\n```\nLevel 1: Session Transcripts (完整上下文，直接索引)\n    ↓ 提取\nLevel 2: Memory (每日摘要，关键决策)\n    ↓ 整理\nLevel 3: Knowledge Base (结构化知识，可复用)\n```\n\n三层都要可搜索，session 不能丢上下文。\n\n**实现路径**：\n\n1. **装 QMD** → 解决 session 直接索引\n2. **配 Ollama embedding** → 解决语义搜索\n3. **整理 knowledge 目录结构** → 结构化知识库\n\n我现在开始装 QMD + Ollama？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":991,"output":535,"cacheRead":75840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77366,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779821513030}}
{"type":"message","id":"14bbb513","parentId":"df17d9e7","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:54:11.942Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e6a8bf8f4a4c4ea01a63e027da\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"sender\": \"VAN\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 02:54 GMT+8\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"VAN (ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_1a64d3ea99c24cac146f8ec1b670f683\",\n  \"name\": \"VAN\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e6a8bf8f4a4c4ea01a63e027da]\nVAN: 在保持现方案稳定顺利运行，可退基础上完整实现。"}],"timestamp":1779821651940}}
{"type":"message","id":"556fd5e3","parentId":"14bbb513","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:54:18.974Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN wants me to implement the three-tier memory system while keeping the current system stable and rollback-able. Let me plan this carefully:\n\n1. Keep current system running (memory-search.sh, auto-memory, etc.)\n2. Install QMD as an optional backend\n3. Install Ollama for embeddings\n4. Configure OpenClaw to use QMD with session indexing\n5. Make it rollback-able (keep current config as backup)\n\nLet me start.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_08290403279d4d99af47706c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 备份当前配置\ncp /workspace/projects/openclaw.json /workspace/projects/openclaw.json.bak-memory-$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M)\necho \"✅ 配置已备份\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":649,"output":254,"cacheRead":76800,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77703,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779821651942}}
