{"type":"message","id":"6a0455d6","parentId":"c5024eb0","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:59:09.706Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check the QMD docs more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b1c4f080c9604a19a994c6f0","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"export BUN_INSTALL=\"/root/.bun\"\nexport PATH=\"$BUN_INSTALL/bin:$PATH\"\n\n# 查看 QMD 完整帮助\nqmd embed --help 2>&1\necho \"===\"\n# 检查环境变量\nenv | grep -i \"OPENAI\\|OLLAMA\\|EMBED\" 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":207,"output":115,"cacheRead":85696,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86018,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779821943040}}
{"type":"message","id":"45d781bf","parentId":"6a0455d6","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:59:09.815Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b1c4f080c9604a19a994c6f0","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"qmd — Quick Markdown Search\n\nUsage:\n  qmd <command> [options]\n\nPrimary commands:\n  qmd query <query>             - Hybrid search with auto expansion + reranking (recommended)\n  qmd query 'lex:..\\nvec:...'   - Structured query document (you provide lex/vec/hyde lines)\n  qmd search <query>            - Full-text BM25 keywords (no LLM)\n  qmd vsearch <query>           - Vector similarity only\n  qmd get <file>[:line] [-l N]  - Show a single document, optional line slice\n  qmd multi-get <pattern>       - Batch fetch via glob or comma-separated list\n  qmd skills list/get/path      - List and retrieve bundled runtime skills\n  qmd skill show/install        - Show or install the QMD skill\n  qmd mcp                       - Start the MCP server (stdio transport for AI agents)\n  qmd bench <fixture.json>      - Run search quality benchmarks against a fixture file\n\nCollections & context:\n  qmd collection add/list/remove/rename/show   - Manage indexed folders\n  qmd context add/list/rm                      - Attach human-written summaries\n  qmd ls [collection[/path]]                   - Inspect indexed files\n\nMaintenance:\n  qmd init                      - Create a project-local .qmd index\n  qmd status                    - View index + collection health\n  qmd update [--pull]           - Re-index collections (optionally git pull first)\n  qmd embed [-f] [-c <name>]    - Generate/refresh vector embeddings\n    --max-docs-per-batch <n>    - Cap docs loaded into memory per embedding batch\n    --max-batch-mb <n>          - Cap UTF-8 MB loaded into memory per embedding batch\n  qmd cleanup                   - Clear caches, vacuum DB\n\nQuery syntax (qmd query):\n  QMD queries are either a single expand query (no prefix) or a multi-line\n  document where every line is typed with lex:, vec:, or hyde:. This grammar\n  matches the docs in docs/SYNTAX.md and is enforced in the CLI.\n\n  Grammar:\n    query          = expand_query | query_document ;\n    expand_query   = text | explicit_expand ;\n    explicit_expand= \"expand:\" text ;\n    query_document = [ intent_line ] { typed_line } ;\n    intent_line    = \"intent:\" text newline ;\n    typed_line     = type \":\" text newline ;\n    type           = \"lex\" | \"vec\" | \"hyde\" ;\n    text           = quoted_phrase | plain_text ;\n    quoted_phrase  = '\"' { character } '\"' ;\n    plain_text     = { character } ;\n    newline        = \"\\n\" ;\n\n  Examples:\n    qmd query \"how does auth work\"                # single-line → implicit expand\n    qmd query $'lex: CAP theorem\\nvec: consistency'  # typed query document\n    qmd query $'lex: \"exact matches\" sports -baseball'  # phrase + negation lex search\n    qmd query $'hyde: Hypothetical answer text'       # hyde-only document\n\n  Constraints:\n    - Standalone expand queries cannot mix with typed lines.\n    - Query documents allow only lex:, vec:, or hyde: prefixes.\n    - Each typed line must be single-line text with balanced quotes.\n\nAI agents & integrations:\n  - Run `qmd mcp` to expose the MCP server (stdio) to agents/IDEs.\n  - Run `qmd skills get qmd --full` for version-matched agent instructions.\n  - `qmd skill install` installs the QMD skill into ./.agents/skills/qmd.\n  - Use `qmd skill install --global` for ~/.agents/skills/qmd.\n  - `qmd --skill` is kept as an alias for `qmd skill show`.\n  - Advanced: `qmd mcp --http ...` and `qmd mcp --http --daemon` are optional for custom transports.\n\nGlobal options:\n  --index <name>             - Use a named index (default: index)\n  QMD_EDITOR_URI             - Editor link template for clickable TTY search output\n\nSearch options:\n  -n <num>                   - Max results (default 5, or 20 for --files/--json)\n  --all                      - Return all matches (pair with --min-score)\n  --min-score <num>          - Minimum similarity score\n  --full                     - Output full document instead of snippet\n  -C, --candidate-limit <n>  - Max candidates to rerank (default 40, lower = faster)\n  --no-rerank                - Skip LLM reranking (use RRF scores only, much faster on CPU)\n  --no-gpu                   - Force CPU mode for llama.cpp operations (same as QMD_FORCE_CPU=1)\n  --line-numbers             - Include line numbers in output\n  --explain                  - Include retrieval score traces (query --json/CLI)\n  --files | --json | --csv | --md | --xml  - Output format\n  -c, --collection <name>    - Filter by one or more collections\n\nEmbed/query options:\n  --chunk-strategy <auto|regex> - Chunking mode (default: regex; auto uses AST for code files)\n\nMulti-get options:\n  -l <num>                   - Maximum lines per file\n  --max-bytes <num>          - Skip files larger than N bytes (default 10240)\n  --json/--csv/--md/--xml/--files - Same formats as search\n\nIndex: /root/.cache/qmd/index.sqlite\n===\n\n(Command exited with code 1)"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":1,"durationMs":103,"aggregated":"qmd — Quick Markdown Search\n\nUsage:\n  qmd <command> [options]\n\nPrimary commands:\n  qmd query <query>             - Hybrid search with auto expansion + reranking (recommended)\n  qmd query 'lex:..\\nvec:...'   - Structured query document (you provide lex/vec/hyde lines)\n  qmd search <query>            - Full-text BM25 keywords (no LLM)\n  qmd vsearch <query>           - Vector similarity only\n  qmd get <file>[:line] [-l N]  - Show a single document, optional line slice\n  qmd multi-get <pattern>       - Batch fetch via glob or comma-separated list\n  qmd skills list/get/path      - List and retrieve bundled runtime skills\n  qmd skill show/install        - Show or install the QMD skill\n  qmd mcp                       - Start the MCP server (stdio transport for AI agents)\n  qmd bench <fixture.json>      - Run search quality benchmarks against a fixture file\n\nCollections & context:\n  qmd collection add/list/remove/rename/show   - Manage indexed folders\n  qmd context add/list/rm                      - Attach human-written summaries\n  qmd ls [collection[/path]]                   - Inspect indexed files\n\nMaintenance:\n  qmd init                      - Create a project-local .qmd index\n  qmd status                    - View index + collection health\n  qmd update [--pull]           - Re-index collections (optionally git pull first)\n  qmd embed [-f] [-c <name>]    - Generate/refresh vector embeddings\n    --max-docs-per-batch <n>    - Cap docs loaded into memory per embedding batch\n    --max-batch-mb <n>          - Cap UTF-8 MB loaded into memory per embedding batch\n  qmd cleanup                   - Clear caches, vacuum DB\n\nQuery syntax (qmd query):\n  QMD queries are either a single expand query (no prefix) or a multi-line\n  document where every line is typed with lex:, vec:, or hyde:. This grammar\n  matches the docs in docs/SYNTAX.md and is enforced in the CLI.\n\n  Grammar:\n    query          = expand_query | query_document ;\n    expand_query   = text | explicit_expand ;\n    explicit_expand= \"expand:\" text ;\n    query_document = [ intent_line ] { typed_line } ;\n    intent_line    = \"intent:\" text newline ;\n    typed_line     = type \":\" text newline ;\n    type           = \"lex\" | \"vec\" | \"hyde\" ;\n    text           = quoted_phrase | plain_text ;\n    quoted_phrase  = '\"' { character } '\"' ;\n    plain_text     = { character } ;\n    newline        = \"\\n\" ;\n\n  Examples:\n    qmd query \"how does auth work\"                # single-line → implicit expand\n    qmd query $'lex: CAP theorem\\nvec: consistency'  # typed query document\n    qmd query $'lex: \"exact matches\" sports -baseball'  # phrase + negation lex search\n    qmd query $'hyde: Hypothetical answer text'       # hyde-only document\n\n  Constraints:\n    - Standalone expand queries cannot mix with typed lines.\n    - Query documents allow only lex:, vec:, or hyde: prefixes.\n    - Each typed line must be single-line text with balanced quotes.\n\nAI agents & integrations:\n  - Run `qmd mcp` to expose the MCP server (stdio) to agents/IDEs.\n  - Run `qmd skills get qmd --full` for version-matched agent instructions.\n  - `qmd skill install` installs the QMD skill into ./.agents/skills/qmd.\n  - Use `qmd skill install --global` for ~/.agents/skills/qmd.\n  - `qmd --skill` is kept as an alias for `qmd skill show`.\n  - Advanced: `qmd mcp --http ...` and `qmd mcp --http --daemon` are optional for custom transports.\n\nGlobal options:\n  --index <name>             - Use a named index (default: index)\n  QMD_EDITOR_URI             - Editor link template for clickable TTY search output\n\nSearch options:\n  -n <num>                   - Max results (default 5, or 20 for --files/--json)\n  --all                      - Return all matches (pair with --min-score)\n  --min-score <num>          - Minimum similarity score\n  --full                     - Output full document instead of snippet\n  -C, --candidate-limit <n>  - Max candidates to rerank (default 40, lower = faster)\n  --no-rerank                - Skip LLM reranking (use RRF scores only, much faster on CPU)\n  --no-gpu                   - Force CPU mode for llama.cpp operations (same as QMD_FORCE_CPU=1)\n  --line-numbers             - Include line numbers in output\n  --explain                  - Include retrieval score traces (query --json/CLI)\n  --files | --json | --csv | --md | --xml  - Output format\n  -c, --collection <name>    - Filter by one or more collections\n\nEmbed/query options:\n  --chunk-strategy <auto|regex> - Chunking mode (default: regex; auto uses AST for code files)\n\nMulti-get options:\n  -l <num>                   - Maximum lines per file\n  --max-bytes <num>          - Skip files larger than N bytes (default 10240)\n  --json/--csv/--md/--xml/--files - Same formats as search\n\nIndex: /root/.cache/qmd/index.sqlite\n===\n\n(Command exited with code 1)","cwd":"/workspace/projects/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779821949812}}
{"type":"message","id":"1d30b36e","parentId":"45d781bf","timestamp":"2026-05-26T18:59:17.375Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. QMD uses its own SQLite index at `/root/.cache/qmd/index.sqlite`. For embeddings, it uses llama.cpp locally by default. Let me check if it can use Ollama.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1cd535c0167b493a87cf1025","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"export BUN_INSTALL=\"/root/.bun\"\nexport PATH=\"$BUN_INSTALL/bin:$PATH\"\n\n# 检查 QMD 环境变量\ncat /node_modules/@tobilu/qmd/docs/*.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"env\\|ollama\\|OPENAI\\|embed\" | head -20\necho \"===\"\n# 检查 QMD 的 embedding 配置\ngrep -r \"OLLAMA\\|OPENAI\\|embed\" /node_modules/@tobilu/qmd/src/ 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"env\\|config\\|provider\" | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":1340,"output":245,"cacheRead":85888,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":87473,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779821949816}}
