{"type":"message","id":"07be9fa1","parentId":"55db41d9","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:04:20.545Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"VAN is emphasizing stability and rollback capability. Let me check on the QMD embed process and the current state. Let me also think about whether the QMD approach is the right one.\n\nLooking at this more carefully, the QMD approach is getting complex:\n1. QMD needs to download ~300MB GGUF models on CPU (slow)\n2. QMD indexes .md files, not .jsonl sessions\n3. OpenClaw needs to be configured to export sessions as .md for QMD\n\nMeanwhile, the simpler approach would be:\n1. Use Ollama embedding (already working) with OpenClaw's built-in memorySearch\n\n\n2. Convert session JSONL to .md and add to extraPaths\n3. Keep everything in the existing infrastructure\n\nBut VAN specifically asked for the three-tier system with session indexing. Let me check if QMD embed is still running and whether it's worth continuing or if I should pivot to a more straightforward solution that respects his request while being practical.\n\nActually, I should verify whether the gateway restart will break the running unified engine and check on the QMD embed status first.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me check the current state and QMD embed status."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_635ec3ebefd0414f8573adff","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ps aux | grep -E \"qmd|engine|monitor\" | grep -v grep | head -10\necho \"===\"\ntail -5 /tmp/qmd-embed.log 2>/dev/null\necho \"===\"\n# 检查 QMD 模型下载进度\nfind ~/.cache -name \"*.gguf\" 2>/dev/null -exec ls -lh {} \\;"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5","usage":{"input":66251,"output":577,"cacheRead":28672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":95500,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779822252086}}
