{"type":"message","id":"171b76ba","parentId":"4d9c1ede","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:04:26.267Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"QMD embed is still running and appears stuck on \"Gathering information\". The GGUF models haven't been downloaded yet. This is taking too long on CPU.\n\nLet me think about a better approach. VAN wants:\n1. Three-tier memory system (session → memory → knowledge)\n2. All searchable\n3. Session transcripts preserved with full context\n4. Stable, rollback-able\n\nThe QMD approach is problematic because:\n- It needs to download ~300MB GGUF models on CPU (very slow)\n- It runs on CPU with no GPU (slow inference)\n- It's an experimental feature in OpenClaw\n\n\n- A simpler path forward would be using Ollama embeddings instead, which is already set up and running, then converting session transcripts to markdown and adding them to the search paths. This keeps everything within OpenClaw's existing memory infrastructure without the experimental overhead and slow model downloads.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"QMD embed is stuck downloading GGUF models on CPU (no GPU) - too slow. Let me take a simpler approach that VAN will prefer:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_de478fb7a6e74e32b745015f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 杀掉 QMD embed 进程\nkill 284656 284664 2>/dev/null\necho \"✅ QMD embed 已停止 (CPU太慢，不实用)\"\n\n# 验证统一引擎还在运行\nps aux | grep \"engine.py\" | grep -v grep | awk '{print \"✅ 统一引擎 PID:\", $2, \"运行中\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5","usage":{"input":905,"output":511,"cacheRead":94912,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":96328,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779822260622}}
