{"type":"message","id":"49efc497","parentId":"e0dc7daa","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:16:49.422Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The batch is still disabled with failures 0/2. The issue is that Ollama works for single embeddings but the batch process is failing. This could be a timeout issue since CPU-only Ollama is slow for batch operations. \n\nLet me check the OpenClaw Ollama configuration - maybe there's a timeout setting or the issue is that OpenClaw is trying to use the OpenAI-compatible endpoint on Ollama but Ollama's `/v1/embeddings` endpoint might have a different behavior.\n\nActually, looking at the OpenClaw docs again: \"When `memorySearch.provider = \"ollama\"` is set, OpenClaw auto-selects... but it says provider is set to \"ollama\" but the API key was not...\" earlier. Maybe the issue is that OpenClaw's Ollama integration expects a specific configuration format.\n\nLet me check if there's a models.providers.ollama section needed in the config.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Batch still disabled (failures 0/2). The batch embedding is failing. Let me check if Ollama needs to be configured as a provider."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_36bc07c725a64d54b09848bb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# 检查 OpenClaw 是否需要 ollama 作为 provider 配置\ngrep -r \"ollama\" /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md 2>/dev/null | head -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":350,"output":493,"cacheRead":108352,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":109195,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779822998392}}
