{"type":"message","id":"448c0b95","parentId":"64989374","timestamp":"2026-05-26T19:21:32.955Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The indexing keeps failing because it's timing out. The Ollama embedding is working fine via curl, but OpenClaw's internal batch embedding is failing. The issue might be that OpenClaw is trying to do something different with the Ollama provider for memory search embeddings vs the model provider.\n\nLet me look at this differently. The `memorySearch.provider` is set to \"ollama\" which tells OpenClaw to use its built-in Ollama client for embeddings. The model provider config might not be related to the memory search embedding.\n\nLooking at the OpenClaw docs:\n- `memorySearch.provider = \"ollama\"` - this uses OpenClaw's internal Ollama integration\n- The model provider config is for chat/completion models, not embeddings\n\nThe batch is \"disabled (failures 0/2)\" - this means the embedding batch failed twice and is now disabled. The issue could be:\n1. The Ollama endpoint being used is wrong\n2. The model name being used is wrong\n3. Something about the batch size or timeout\n\nLet me check if there's an `OLLAMA_HOST` env var needed, or if there's a specific config for the memory search Ollama provider.\n\nActually, I recall from earlier that the status said \"Memory search provider is set to 'ollama' but the API key was not\" - maybe that was just a warning, not an error.\n\nThe real issue is: embedding batch keeps failing. The Ollama API works directly. Let me try setting the OLLAMA_API_KEY environment variable and also check if there's a specific timeout issue.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the status output more carefully:\n\n```\nProvider: ollama (requested: ollama)\nModel: nomic-embed-text\nIndexed: 0/122 files · 0 chunks\nBatch: disabled (failures 0/2)\n```\n\n\"Batch: disabled\" - this means the batch embedding process has been disabled after 2 failures. The `0/2` might mean 0 successes out of 2 attempts.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the Ollama provider for memory search is different from the models provider. Let me check if `memorySearch.remote` is needed for Ollama config.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The indexing keeps failing. Let me check if `memorySearch.remote` is where the Ollama config needs to go."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b07b8c9811134445ae0021cc","name":"gateway","arguments":{"action":"config.schema.lookup","path":"agents.defaults.memorySearch.remote"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":72604,"output":1004,"cacheRead":36864,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":110472,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779823274205}}
